   "text": "I read the structure in four parts and then assembled them.\n\n- **Left benzene ring:** it carries the nitrile. Its two neighbouring ring carbons carry a CH2CH2\u2013O chain and a CH2\u2013O chain.\n- **Macrocycle:**\n  - The CH2CH2\u2013O chain ends in an ether O that bonds through a CH2 to the central benzene.\n  - The CH2\u2013O chain ends in an O on C2 of the pyridine.\n  - Pyridine C6 is bonded to the central benzene, meta to the carbon bearing the CH2\u2013O.\n- **Central benzene:** the carbon ortho to the CH2\u2013O carbon carries a CH2 that links to C2 of the benzimidazole.\n- **Benzimidazole:**\n  - N1 carries a CH2 attached to an oxetan-2-yl group.\n  - C4 carries OCH2CH2OCH3.\n  - C6 carries CO2Me.\n\nThe only stereocentre drawn with a hashed bond is oxetane C2. I took the hashed CH2\u2013N bond as pointing behind the plane, which puts H toward the viewer. The CIP priorities are O > CH2N > ring CH2 > H. Tracing O \u2192 CH2N \u2192 ring CH2 on the drawing gives clockwise, and reversing for the H toward the viewer gives counterclockwise, so the centre is S. In the SMILES, the neighbour order CH2N, H, O, CH2 makes `@@` the S form.\n\nI checked that the ring-closure digits pair up correctly and that each atom's connectivity matches the drawing.\n\nSMILES: N#Cc1ccc2c(c1)CCOCc1cc(ccc1Cc1nc3c(OCCOC)cc(C(=O)OC)cc3n1C[C@@H]1CCO1)-c1cccc(n1)OC2"
